 sentence for crimes against humanity. Pumla Gobodo-Madikizela, who grew up in a black township in South Africa served as a psychologist on that country's great national experiment in healing, the Truth and Reconciliation Commission. As this book opens, in an act of inescapable, multilayered symbolism and extraordinary psychological courage, Gobodo-Madikizela enters Pretoria's maximum security prison to meet the man called \"Prime Evil.\" What follows is a journey into what it means to be human.\".","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-a-human-being-died-that-night-pumla-gobodo-madikizela.jpg","renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":45,"criticalRenown":78,"controversy":38,"llmAffinity":88,"affinityResidual":9.76,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.92,"criticalRenown":0.9,"controversy":0.82,"llmAffinity":0.96},"tags":{"craft":"voice","evidence":"interviews-fieldwork","stance":"moral-seriousness"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Eugene de Kock","confidence":0.99}],"centralPlaces":[{"name":"South Africa","confidence":0.95},{"name":"Pretoria","confidence":0.9}],"argument":{"present":false,"statement":"","confidence":0},"academicOrientation":{"score":32,"confidence":0.84},"profileConfidence":0.94,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"argument":{"statement":"Confronting a perpetrator of apartheid violence becomes an exploration of human identity, moral complexity, and the possibility of psychological healing.","confidence":0.52}},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"7e872f73cf5f9358273ecc4b5522f53ac713d9aca9e44a8c48f36c147db573e3","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"displaySummary":"As this book opens, in an act of inescapable, multilayered symbolism and extraordinary psychological courage, Gobodo-Madikizela enters Pretoria's maximum security prison to meet the man called \"Prime Evil.\" What follows is a journey into what it means to be human.\".","primarySubject":"World History",